-  slug: "the-markdown-parser-came-into-akasha-whole-with-three-look-alikes-that-are-not-swaps",
-  domainSlug: "domain/akasha",
-  claim:
-    "The old markdown pages parser and shape checker is inside akasha as `@akasha/markdown-pages`, carried whole rather than left to die with the markdown pages. Its 58 modules cover what the root `page/` directory held: the document parser and shape checker, frontmatter, the property registry, the file tree, globs, the beside-file and uncommitted-sidecar machinery, and `page-types`. Akasha modules and `tools/lib` both read it by package name. The shapes it parses into still come from `@akasha/pages-system/markdown-document`, which holds those types and nothing that parses.",
-  evidence:
-    "`page/` no longer stands at the repo root. `akasha/markdown-pages` holds 58 module folders, one `*.module.code.ts` in each, and a `package.json` exporting all 58 by name.\n\nTHE THREE DIVISIONS OF THE OLD DIRECTORY, AND WHERE EACH WENT. The document parser and checker of `.md` bodies is `markdown-document-tokens`, `-position`, `-holes`, `-shape`, `-template`, `-value` and `-frontmatter`, each still taking its `Document`, `Inline`, `Span` and `Verdict` types from `@akasha/pages-system/markdown-document`. The beside-file and frontmatter machinery is `markdown-attachment-file`, `-rows-file`, `-sidecar`, `-uncommitted`, `-frontmatter`, `-text-at`, `-prose`, `-tracked` and the `markdown-property-*` family. The scaffolding of the markdown world is `markdown-page-types`, `-file-tree`, `-glob`, `-repo-claim`, `-page-address`, `-runtime-mark`, `-shape-mark` and `-file-carries-bytes`.\n\nTHREE HAVE A PAGES-SYSTEM MODULE DOING THE SAME JOB, MATCHED AT THE JOB RATHER THAN EXPORT FOR EXPORT, SO NEITHER IS A SWAP A CALLER MAY TAKE ON TRUST: `markdown-page-address` against `akasha/pages-system/pages/address/page-address.module.code.ts`, `markdown-uncommitted` against `akasha/pages-system/pages/uncommitted/page-uncommitted.module.code.ts`, and `markdown-sidecar` against `akasha/pages-system/pages/beside/page-beside.module.code.ts`. The markdown half reads `.md` pages and their yaml sidecars; the pages-system half reads `.ts` pages. Choosing by name reads nothing rather than failing.\n\nThe two modules that once reached out of akasha for this machinery now take it by package name: `editor-page-sweeping.module.code.ts:1` and `:3`, and `royal-road-syncing.module.code.ts:3`. `tools/lib` reaches the same package rather than a relative climb.",
-} as const satisfies Finding
